Subject: expr.c: drop OpenBSD pledge() call

pledge(2) is OpenBSD-specific.  Substrate has no equivalent
sandboxing call; the relevant kernel-side protections are
provided by the personality + LSM hooks elsewhere.

---
diff -urN a/expr.c b/expr.c
--- a/expr.c
+++ b/expr.c
@@ -495,9 +495,6 @@
 {
 	struct val     *vp;

-	if (pledge("stdio", NULL) == -1)
-		err(2, "pledge");
-
 	if (argc > 1 && !strcmp(argv[1], "--"))
 		argv++;

